  You're right.  The #enhance screen is an out-of-game redundant
player decision that can only reflect decisions the player has already
made in-game.  It's also redundant in that roles already have limited
skill levels.  If player characteristics like Str, Dx, Co, In, etc.
can be increased/decreased irrespective of XL there's no reason weapon
and spell skills can't.

  There's no need for weapon/spell skills to decay.  Only one, or at
most two, weapons can be used at one time.  Carrying around every
weapon the character can increase skill in would be its own punishment
in terms of weight.  Spells are limited by mana, which is itself
already mostly dependent on XL.  Spell failure rates are also already
affected by XL.  Again, skill slots based on XL are redundant.

  So automatically #enhance skills when they've been exercised enough.
just keep the #enhance screen so the player can check what skills are
possible for the role and what level has been achieved.



